<title>AUSTRALIA: Placer year net falls to A$43.5 mln.</title>
<headline>Placer year net falls to A$43.5 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31</p>
<p>	    (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			  43.5 vs  58.6</p>
<p>NOTE: Placer Pacific Ltd is a gold miner and is controlled by Placer Dome Inc, which has offered to buy out the remaining shares it does not already own in the Australian group.  </p>
<p>    Operating profit		     82.5 vs 123.2</p>
<p>    Abnormal items			  nil vs loss 10.7</p>
<p>    Tax					34.8 vs  43.0</p>
<p>    Interest				  3.3 vs   6.8</p>
<p>    Minorities				4.2 vs 10.9</p>
<p>NOTE: The results were released as part of an independent expert report on Placer Pacific by Grant Samuel as part of the group's evaluation of the mop-up bid by Placer Dome.</p>
<p>Placer Pacific said a preliminary final report would be released to the market on February 13, which would include all the financial figures for the group.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
